# Trivy ignore-list policy (docs/modernization-roadmap.md F45, epic #10,
# #59 WS2.4, #59 risk 3).
#
# What belongs here: confirmed false positives, and CVEs reviewed and
# deliberately deferred -- each entry MUST carry a one-line rationale
# comment. Never add an entry silently.
#
# What does NOT belong here: a CVE just because it's noisy. Every workflow
# that references this file runs Trivy non-blocking (`exit-code: 0`,
# `continue-on-error: true`), specifically so real findings stay visible
# without gating anything -- see F45's "red is signal, not noise" framing.
# Blanket-allowlisting a fixable CVE defeats the point of shipping this
# scanner in the first place.
#
# Do NOT add entries here to suppress yt-dlp / ytmusicapi findings
# (services/ytmusic-streamer). Those pins are deliberately loose so
# YouTube-breakage fixes land fast; Dependabot/Trivy pressure on them is
# wanted, not something to silence. See .github/dependabot.yml's header.
#
# --- Day-one filesystem baseline (2026-07-10, cycle 2 / packet E) ----------
# Command (from a clean worktree at commit 796dacd / 1.8.0):
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/repo" aquasec/trivy fs \
#     --severity CRITICAL,HIGH --ignore-unfixed /repo
#
# Result: 49 findings, all HIGH (0 CRITICAL), all with a fixed version
# already published (Status: fixed) -- i.e. every one of them is a real,
# Dependabot-actionable finding, not noise:
#   - backend/package-lock.json (31): axios, defu, effect,
#     express-rate-limit, form-data, lodash, minimatch, multer,
#     music-metadata, path-to-regexp, socket.io-parser, ws
#   - frontend/package-lock.json (18): @xmldom/xmldom,
#     http-proxy-middleware, next, picomatch, socket.io-parser, ws
#
# None of these 49 were allowlisted. They're left as the intended day-one
# visible baseline; expect most to clear as the weekly grouped Dependabot
# PRs (.github/dependabot.yml) land minor/patch bumps. Re-triage individual
# CVE IDs into this file (with rationale) only if a specific one turns out
# to be a false positive or a deliberate, reasoned "not fixing this now".
#
# --- Anticipated (not yet seeded) base-image baseline -----------------------
# services/audio-analyzer/Dockerfile is `FROM ubuntu:20.04` (EOL) and
# audio-analyzer-clap pulls in torch/torchaudio/torchvision -- both will
# carry unfixable-in-place CVEs once trivy-image actually scans the built
# GHCR images (schedule/workflow_dispatch only, see
# .github/workflows/image-security-scanning.yml). This worktree can't build all
# 8 images to pre-seed that baseline, so nothing has been added for it yet.
# Add entries here with rationale (CVE ID + why it's unfixable/accepted) the
# first time that job actually reports something -- don't invent CVE IDs
# speculatively.
#
# Syntax: one CVE-ID / GHSA-ID per line, optional trailing comment. See
# https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
